  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The equation of the hyperbola $18{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}=90$ in standard form is{{field-1}}\n$=1.$",
  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $90$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}18{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2} & =90 \\\\ \\frac{18{x}^{2}}{90}-\\frac{5{y}^{2}}{90} & =\\frac{90}{90} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{18} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
